Using NAMELIST input for the 1D Hartree-Fock code:
--------------------------------------------------

Code Update 21. March 2026


The input data for the 1D code can now be given as
a Fortran namelist. The structure is the same as
for the 2D SkyAx code. But several input parameters
differ for technoical reasons. Here a brief summary
of input parameters:

Namelist &MAIN:

 title       = character array with title of the run
 iwunit      = output switch 
                0: to file 'for006', 1: to std output, -1: terminate
 itmax       = number of static iterations
 iwr         = print level to std output (from -2 to +1)
 ifplot      = level of compressed output on 'for011' 
               the larger the more, recommended value ifplot=3
 iterbcs     = nr. of initial BCS iterations in HFB run
 iterhfb     = nr. of steps with enhanced pairing strength in HFB run
 pairenhance = initial enhancement factor on pairing strength, the factor 
               is reduced linearly until step nr. 'iterhfb' is reached
 modnat      = modulus of calling 'hfb_natural' which is the routine
               for the HFB step in configuration space
 iternat     = number of sub-iterations in  'hfb_natural'
 v2limh      = lower limit of occupation 'v**2' in HFB Hamiltonian
 delmix      = mixing factor of old and new occupations in HFB
 tnobcs      = inactive in 1D


Namelist &GRIDS:

 ngrid       = number of radial grid points
 rstep       = grid spacing


Namelist &STATIC:

 nprot       = nr. of protons
 nneut       = nr. of neutrons
 nmaxp       = nr. of proton j-shells 
 nmaxn       = nr. of neutron j-shells 
 deocc       = two entries as nr. of proton and neutron extra shells,
               value will be converted to nearest integer,
               must not exceed 6
 e0inv       = damping energy in damped gradient step
 x0inv       = dimensionless step size in damped gradient step
 addrho      = admixture of new density, density is composed as 
                'addrho'*rho_new+(1.'addrho')*rh_old
 addpot      = obsolete in 1D code
 addocc      = obsolete in 1D code
 errenr      = termination criterion for energy convergence
 errrad      = termination criterion for radius convergence
 npiter      = nr. of pairing iterations
 trestart    = solutions will recycled if .TRUE. (not so useful
               in single runs)


Namelist &FORCE:

 This provides the force parameters and options. It is the same 
 as in the 2D code SkyAx.
 Note that only the option 'istsym=0' is implemented ('istsym'
 choses the level of treatment of spin terms). In the 1D code
 it means that the full time-odd terms are active for odd nuclei,
 but that Cramer's degeneracy is maintained. 


Namelist &THERMAL:

 temprt      = posibly finite temperature



Sample input is provided in
  test/for005.SVbas.nameinp for the Skymre foirce SV-bas  and
  test/for005.FyIVP.namelinp for the Fayans model Fy(IVP).
The files
  test/for005.SVbas and
  test/for005.FyIVP
are input in old standard form for the same cases.